-This first checkpoint supports the native panel link and an uncorrected per-eye view.
-The receiver reads native pixels, refresh and scale from KScreen rather than treating Qt's logical window dimensions as panel pixels.
+The receiver offers the native panel link and the four 720p packing choices.
+It reads native pixels, refresh, scale and physical size from KScreen and its connected screen.
+The resulting transport raster determines the RDP stream size.
 It uses ordinary Qt Quick on a mono output and does not require Stereo KWin on the receiving device.
 The sender requires the native-panel KRdp and Stereo KWin extensions.
 
 The current-frame handoff makes an owned copy on the FreeRDP worker before it can overwrite its GDI buffer.
 There is one pending frame and one queued notification; a newer frame replaces an unconsumed one.
 Qt Quick fits each eye using the current image dimensions at every paint.
-ARM hardware decoding, the paired KDE Connect handoff, optical profiles, movies, sensors and the native compositor output choice are subsequent checkpoints.
+ARM hardware decoding, optical profiles, movies, sensors and the native compositor output choice are subsequent checkpoints.
 An amd64 proof does not qualify a physical phone's decoder or optics.
 
 `-DCATCH_PROOF=ON` enables private-session capture and deliberate eye-swap, frozen-frame and certificate-pin controls.
